  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency shelter and non-food item (NFI) assistance to flood-affected people in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this IOM project is to immediately scale up the response to address the most pressing needs of the flood-affected population, prioritizing the most vulnerable groups in Garissa, Kilifi, Homa Bay, Tana River, and Nairobi counties. The project provides emergency shelters and non-food items, raises awareness on protection mainstreaming, and conducts post-distribution monitoring. The project aims to assist 20,500 people, including 3,690 men, 3,894 women, 12,916 children, and 459 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
